          "targetAge": "3.5-4",
          "text": "Does the child demonstrate the ability to hop on one foot with balance?",
          "activities": [
            "One-Foot Hop Challenge – Demonstrate hopping on one foot for 2-3 hops. Encourage the child to try hopping on one foot (allow support at first). Observe if the child can maintain balance and hop at least 2 times. Purpose: Assesses balance, leg strength, and single-leg stability. Hop to the Target – Place a target (toy or marker) a short distance away. Encourage the child to hop on one foot towards the target. Observe if the child can maintain balance while moving forward. Purpose: Assesses dynamic balance, body control, and directional movement. Copy the Animal – Pretend to be hopping animals: \"Hop like a kangaroo!\" or \"Hop like a frog!\" Encourage the child to imitate the animal movements. Observe if the child can maintain the hop and show creativity. Purpose: Assesses imagination, gross motor skills, and imitation."
          ],
