          "milestone": "Follows simple safety rules",
          "targetAge": "3.5-4",
          "text": "Does the child demonstrate understanding and compliance with basic safety rules during physical activities?",
          "activities": [
            "Safety Rule Discussion – Discuss simple safety rules: \"We walk when carrying objects\" and \"We look before we run.\" Practice each rule in the appropriate setting. Observe if the child remembers and follows the rules. Purpose: Assesses understanding of rules, memory, and self-regulation. Role-Play Safety Scenarios – Create scenarios: \"What should you do if someone gets hurt?\" Encourage the child to role-play the safe response. Observe if the child can identify and demonstrate safe choices. Purpose: Assesses problem-solving, understanding, and application of safety knowledge. Safe Movement Practice – During play, remind the child: \"Remember, we walk when we carry heavy objects.\" Observe if the child adjusts behavior based on the reminder. Note if the child requires repeated reminders or self-corrects. Purpose: Assesses listening skills, rule-following, and impulse control."
          ],
